{{!
    @template enrol_apply/groupkey_item

    One keyed group of enrol_apply/groupkey_summary: its name, its seats when known, and what is
    wrong with its key, inside the list item the caller writes. The key itself is never in the
    context.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * name string - the group name, plain spelling
    * hasseats boolean - whether seats are known (local_groupdist is installed)
    * nolimit boolean - whether the group declares no seats
    * members int - current members
    * seats int - declared seats
    * full boolean - whether no seat is left, so the key admits nobody now
    * isshadowed boolean - whether another group the reader may see shares this key and admits instead
    * shadowedby string - the name of that group, or empty
    * untypable boolean - whether the key starts or ends with a space

    Example context (json):
    {"name": "Turma C", "hasseats": true, "nolimit": true, "members": 8, "seats": 0,
     "full": false, "isshadowed": true, "shadowedby": "Turma A", "untypable": false}
}}
<span class="fw-bold">{{name}}</span>
{{#hasseats}}
    {{#nolimit}}
        <span class="text-muted">&middot; {{#str}} groupseatsnolimit, enrol_apply, {{members}} {{/str}}</span>
    {{/nolimit}}
    {{^nolimit}}
        <span class="text-muted">&middot; {{#str}} groupseatsof, enrol_apply, { "members": {{members}}, "seats": {{seats}} } {{/str}}</span>
    {{/nolimit}}
    {{#full}}
        <span class="badge bg-warning text-dark">{{#str}} groupkeyadmitsnobody, enrol_apply {{/str}}</span>
    {{/full}}
{{/hasseats}}
{{#isshadowed}}
    <div class="small text-muted">{{#str}} groupkeyshadowed, enrol_apply, {{shadowedby}} {{/str}}</div>
{{/isshadowed}}
{{#untypable}}
    <div class="small text-muted">{{#str}} groupkeyuntypable, enrol_apply {{/str}}</div>
{{/untypable}}
